#: Intro.md:1
msgid "PathCVs background & overview"
msgstr "Path CV の背景と概要"

#: Intro.md:3
msgid ""
"Path Collective Variables (Path CVs) are designed to describe complex "
"molecular transitions that are difficult to capture with a limited number of"
" standard collective variables (https://doi.org/10.1063/1.2432340). The "
"putative reaction coordinate is therefore mapped using two CVs, which are "
"functions of the configurational space $\\mathbf{R}$:"
msgstr ""
"Path Collective Variables (Path CVs) は、少数の標準 CV "
"では捉えにくい複雑な分子遷移を記述します（https://doi.org/10.1063/1.2432340）。推定 Reaction "
"Coordinate は、Configuration 空間 $\\mathbf{R}$ の関数である2つの CV で写像します。"

# Literal notation or identifier intentionally preserved.
#: Intro.md:5
msgid ""
"$S(\\mathbf{R})=\\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^{N}i\\text{e}^{-\\lambda "
"(\\mathbf{R}-\\mathbf{R}(i))^{2}}}{\\sum_{i=1}^{N}\\text{e}^{-\\lambda "
"(\\mathbf{R}-\\mathbf{R}(i))^{2}}}$"
msgstr ""
"$S(\\mathbf{R})=\\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^{N}i\\text{e}^{-\\lambda "
"(\\mathbf{R}-\\mathbf{R}(i))^{2}}}{\\sum_{i=1}^{N}\\text{e}^{-\\lambda "
"(\\mathbf{R}-\\mathbf{R}(i))^{2}}}$"

# Literal notation or identifier intentionally preserved.
#: Intro.md:7
msgid ""
"$Z(\\mathbf{R})=-\\frac{1}{\\lambda}\\ln{\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{N}\\text{e}^{-\\lambda"
" (\\mathbf{R}-\\mathbf{R}(i))^{2}}\\right)}$"
msgstr ""
"$Z(\\mathbf{R})=-\\frac{1}{\\lambda}\\ln{\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{N}\\text{e}^{-\\lambda"
" (\\mathbf{R}-\\mathbf{R}(i))^{2}}\\right)}$"

#: Intro.md:9
msgid ""
"where $i$ is an index ranging from $1$ to $N$. In this framework, "
"$S(\\mathbf{R})$ represents the progression along the guessed path from the "
"initial to the final reference state, while $Z(\\mathbf{R})$ measures the "
"distance from it, providing the path with a certain degree of non-locality. "
"Notably, both the initial and final states should correspond to "
"thermodynamically stable minima, and should be known in advance."
msgstr ""
"$i$ は $1$〜$N$ の Index です。$S(\\mathbf{R})$ は初期から最終参照状態への推定 Path "
"に沿う進行度、$Z(\\mathbf{R})$ は Path "
"からの距離を表し、ある程度の非局所性を与えます。初期・最終状態はいずれも熱力学的に安定な極小で、事前にわかっている必要があります。"

#: Intro.md:11
msgid ""
"Path CVs must be parameterized in terms of a set of $N$ nodes (or frames) "
"which provide a discrete representation of the reaction coordinate to be "
"described. In their original implementation, "
"$\\left(\\mathbf{R}-\\mathbf{R}(i)\\right)^{2}$ is calculated as the mean "
"squared displacement (MSD) in the Cartesian space for a subset of atoms of "
"the system, though alternative metrics may be employed. Finally, $\\lambda$ "
"is a tunable parameter that controls the smoothness of the mapping from the "
"configurational space to the current set of frames (or frameset)."
msgstr ""
"Path CV は、Reaction Coordinate を離散的に表す $N$ Node（Frame）でパラメータ化します。元の実装では "
"$\\left(\\mathbf{R}-\\mathbf{R}(i)\\right)^{2}$ は原子の部分集合の Cartesian MSD "
"ですが、別の Metric も使えます。$\\lambda$ は、Configuration 空間から Frameset "
"への写像の滑らかさを調整するパラメータです。"

#: Intro.md:13
msgid "For Path CVs to be effective, a set of conditions must be met:"
msgstr "Path CV が有効であるには、次が必要です。"

#: Intro.md:14
msgid ""
"The nodal points $\\mathbf{R}(i)$ in the frameset should be as equidistant "
"as possible"
msgstr "Frameset の Node $\\mathbf{R}(i)$ が可能な限り等間隔である。"

#: Intro.md:15
msgid ""
"$\\lambda$ should be commensurate with the inverse of the mean squared "
"displacement between consecutive frames"
msgstr "$\\lambda$ が隣接 Frame 間 MSD の逆数に見合う。"

#: Intro.md:16
msgid ""
"The frameset used to describe the reaction coordinate must provide a good "
"approximation of the minimum free energy pathway from the initial and final "
"reference states"
msgstr "Frameset が初期・最終参照状態間の Minimum Free Energy Pathway をよく近似する。"

#: Intro.md:18
msgid ""
"The third condition pertains to how accurately the parameterized "
"$S(\\mathbf{R})$ reflects the actual reaction coordinate, which can be "
"addressed through variational optimization procedures. In contrast, points 1"
" and 2 concern with the proper parameterization of the guessed path, "
"regardless of its physical relevance. Although primarily technical, these "
"points significantly affect the quality of the resulting Path CVs, "
"especially in the case of resampling efforts."
msgstr ""
"3番目は $S(\\mathbf{R})$ が実際の Reaction Coordinate "
"をどれほど正確に表すかで、変分最適化で対処できます。一方1・2は、物理的妥当性によらず推定 Path "
"を適切にパラメータ化する条件です。技術的ですが、特に再 Sampling 時の Path CV の質を大きく左右します。"

#: Intro.md:20
msgid ""
"Consider, for instance, a path composed of five perfectly equidistant "
"frames, where each frame is a function of the coordinate $x$ only, for "
"simplicity. The variable $S(x)$ can be viewed as a normalized sum of "
"Gaussian functions, with same width (determined by $\\lambda$) but varying "
"heights. As **Figure 1** shows, a proper choice of $\\lambda$ results in a "
"smooth mapping of $S(x)$ (black line). Conversely, if one had chosen an "
"incorrect $\\lambda$ value, such as one that is too large relative to the "
"optimal range, the result would resemble the situation shown in **Figure "
"2**. In this case, the mapping is insufficiently smooth, potentially causing"
" artifacts in the dynamics or even in the resulting free energy surface, "
"when such a path is applied in metadynamics resampling."
msgstr ""
"例えば、座標 $x$ のみの関数である等間隔の5 Frame を考えます。$S(x)$ は、幅（$\\lambda$ が決定）が同じで高さが異なる "
"Gaussian の正規化した和と見なせます。**図1** の適切な $\\lambda$ は滑らかな "
"$S(x)$（黒線）を与えます。最適範囲より大きすぎるなど、不適切な $\\lambda$ では **図2** "
"のようになります。写像が十分滑らかでないため、Metadynamics による再 Sampling の Dynamics や自由エネルギー表面に "
"Artifact が生じる可能性があります。"

#: Intro.md:24
msgid "![path](figures/NewPath_Figure_three_panels.png \"Figure\")"
msgstr "![Path](figures/NewPath_Figure_three_panels.png \"Figure\")"

#: Intro.md:26
msgid "As a rule of thumb, $\\lambda$ shoud be chosen according to:"
msgstr "$\\lambda$ の選択の目安は、"

# Literal notation or identifier intentionally preserved.
#: Intro.md:28
msgid "$\\lambda=-\\frac{\\ln{0.1}}{\\langle MSD\\rangle}$"
msgstr "$\\lambda=-\\frac{\\ln{0.1}}{\\langle MSD\\rangle}$"

#: Intro.md:30
msgid ""
"where $\\langle MSD\\rangle$ is the average MSD evaluated along the entire "
"frameset."
msgstr "$\\langle MSD\\rangle$ は Frameset 全体の平均 MSD です。"

#: Intro.md:32
msgid ""
"However, in practical applications, particularly when the path is "
"parameterized using previously sampled configurations, satisfying the "
"equidistance condition is not trivial, and one often runs into a situation "
"like the one shown **Figure 3**. Note that in this case, the value of "
"$\\lambda$ is indeed consistent with the inverse of the average MSD (i.e. "
"the rule of thumb for $\\lambda$ applies). Nevertheless, the failure to "
"maintain sufficiently equidistant consecutive frames leads to poor behavior "
"of $S(x)$, as illustrated in the plot."
msgstr ""
"ただし実際には、特に既存の Configuration を使う場合、等間隔条件は容易に満たせず、**図3** の状況になりがちです。$\\lambda$"
" は平均 MSD の逆数と整合し、$\\lambda$ の目安を満たしますが、隣接 Frame が十分等間隔でないため、$S(x)$ "
"の挙動が悪くなります。"

#: Intro.md:34
msgid ""
"This tutorial focuses on the parameterization of an initial guess path for a"
" drug-target complex binding, using steered MD simulations to generate the "
"initial frameset, and starting from the bound state of the complex. For the "
"generation of the initial guess path we will make use of Tcl scripts kindly "
"provided by the author of the method (<u>Davide Branduardi</u>)."
msgstr ""
"この Tutorial では薬物・標的複合体の結合状態から Steered MD で初期 Frameset を作り、推定 Path "
"をパラメータ化します。手法の著者 <u>Davide Branduardi</u> が提供した Tcl スクリプトを使います。"

#: Intro.md:36
msgid ""
"At "
"[this](https://github.com/mbernett/zip_for_tutorials/tree/master/analysis_path_tutorial.ipynb)"
" link we provide a Jupyter Notebook to reproduce the plots shown in this "
"tutorial. We also provide inputs to run the simulations, as well as a "
"[sample output "
"trajectory](https://github.com/mbernett/zip_for_tutorials/tree/master/tutorial_binding_path_outputs/SMD_50ns)"
" from steered MD."
msgstr ""
"図を再現する Jupyter Notebook は "
"[こちら](https://github.com/mbernett/zip_for_tutorials/tree/master/analysis_path_tutorial.ipynb)"
" にあります。シミュレーション入力と Steered MD の "
"[出力例](https://github.com/mbernett/zip_for_tutorials/tree/master/tutorial_binding_path_outputs/SMD_50ns)"
" もあります。"
